n","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"RŪmī's sufi ecumenism \"one shrine alone\": Christians, sufis, and the vision of Mawlānā / Roderick Grierson","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"The contemporary relevance of Rūmī's language of the soul / Kabir Helminski","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Historical and theological perspectives on Rūmī's oeuvre: towards a chronology of the poems in the Dīvān-i shams: A prolegomenon for a periodization of Rūmī's literary oeuvre / Franklin Lewis","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"The revival of the spiritual dimension of the sunna in Rūmī's Mathnawī / Shahram Pazouki","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"From Rūmī's Mathnawī to the popular stage / Iraj Anvar & Peter Chelkowski","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Designs of love: sense and structure in Rūmī's Mathnawī","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Open heart surgery: the poetic operation of love in Rūmī's mathnawī / Alan Williams","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"The ascension of the word: rhetoric and reader engagement in Rūmī's Mathnawī / James W. Morris","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Wakened by the dove's trill: structure and meaning in the preface to Rūmī's Mathnawī, book IV / Carl W. Ernst)","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Spiritual progression in books one and two of the Mathnawī / Simon Weightman","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"In memoriam: Gökalp Kâmil / Roderick Grierson.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"series":["The library of perennial philosophy","Spiritual masters : East & West series","Library of perennial philosophy"],"local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223112129623","urn:sfpl:31223112129631"],"lc_classifications":["PK6482 .P45 2014","PK6482.P45 2014"],"key":"/books/OL27170936M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL509133A","name":"Leonard Lewisohn"}],"subtitle":"Rumi and the Sufi tradition","subjects":["Sufism","Persian Sufi poetry","History and criticism","Criticism and interpretation","Mevleviyeh","History"],"isbn_13":["9781936597420"],"pagination":"xxii, 319 pages","source_records":["marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run05.mrc:115138233:3517","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part41.utf8:194711111:2414","bwb:9781936597420","amazon:193659742X","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.14.20150123.full.mrc:358473157:2682","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_006.bib.mrc:258492866:5387"],"title":"The philosophy of ecstasy","dewey_decimal_class":["891/.5511"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (page 285-306) and index."},"number_of_pages":319,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lccn":["2014036150"],"isbn_10":["193659742X"],"subject_people":["Jalāl al-Dīn Rūmī Maulana (1207-1273)"],"publish_country":"inu","publish_date":"2014","by_statement":"edited by Leonard Lewisohn","oclc_numbers":["879582691"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL19990823W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"publishers":["Tradeselect Limited","World Wisdom","Tradeselect"],"covers":[13740975],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Jalal al-Din Rumi (1207-73), founder of the Mevlevi Sufi order of \"Whirling Dervishes,\" is the best-selling poet in America today. The wide-ranging appeal of his work is such that UNESCO declared 2007 to be \"International Rumi Year.\" However, his writings represent much more than love poetry. Rumi was one of the preeminent thinkers of Sufism, the esoteric form of Islam. In this groundbreaking collection of 13 essays on Rumi, many of the world's leading authorities in the field of Islamic Studies and Persian Literature discuss the major religious themes in his poetry and teachings. In addition to discussing the ideas of love, ecstasy, and music in Rumi's Sufi poetry, the essays offer new historical and theological perspectives on his work. The immortality of the soul, freewill, the nature of punishment and reward, and the relationship of Islam to Christianity are all covered, in order to bring Rumi's poetry properly into the context of the Sufi tradition to which he belonged."},"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-07-18T17:18:46.453790"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-06-30T05:15:38.801119"}}},"ISBN:9780307587732":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780307587732","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27127625M/Saved_by_beauty","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/savedbybeautyadv0000hous","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9690992-S.jpg","details":{"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Poet, adventurer, and unapologetic romantic Housden travels to Iran to learn about the people, the culture, and the art of this misunderstood land."},"title":"Saved by beauty","subtitle":"adventures of an American romantic in Iran","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL375002A","name":"Roger Housden"}],"publish_date":"2011","publishers":["Broadway Books"],"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Writing Iran","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Leaving the known","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Paradise and poetry","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Talking stones","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Return to the source","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"The blue dome","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","